<!-- src/components/common/WolffieLogo.vue
 *
 * Inlined so `currentColor` can see the page CSS. Loaded as <img> or as a
 * background-image the SVG is a separate document, `color` falls back to its
 * initial value, and the mark renders black on every theme.
 *
 * Colour comes from the CSS `color` of this element or any ancestor:
 *   <WolffieLogo class="w-8 text-primary" />
 *   <WolffieLogo :style="{ color: 'var(--color-accent)' }" />
 *
 * Sizing is CSS-only. There is deliberately no width/height attribute, so
 * set a width on the element and the aspect ratio follows from the viewBox.
 *
 * The two shading paths use currentColor at fixed opacity rather than their
 * original #3E3E3E / #D7D7D7. Opacity blends toward whatever is behind the
 * mark, so the shading darkens on dark themes and lightens on light ones
 * automatically — no per-theme rules, and it works for presets not yet added.
 -->
